        "original_id": "40a6989a-556c-5bbe-b8b1-39b8c3daa41f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dan Schneider, Helen Hunt\n- Companies: Schneider's Bakery\n- Roles: actor, television writer, film writer, producer, actress, director, screenwriter\n- Products: All That, The Amanda Show, What I Like About You, Drake & Josh, Zoey 101, iCarly, Victorious, Sam & Cat, Henry Danger, Game Shakers, The Adventures of Kid Danger and Captain Man, Mad About You, As Good as It Gets\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Actress, Emmy Awards, Golden Globe Awards, Screen Actors Guild Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Dan Schneider was born on January 14, 1966, and he is an American actor, television and film writer, and producer.\n- Helen Hunt was born on June 15, 1963, and she is an American actress, director, and screenwriter.\n- Dan Schneider appeared mostly in supporting roles in a number of 1980s and 1990s films and TV shows before devoting himself to behind-the-scenes production work.\n- Helen Hunt starred in the sitcom Mad About You for seven years.\n- Helen Hunt played Carol Connelly, a single mother, in the 1997 romantic comedy film As Good as It Gets and won the Academy Award for Best Actress for that role.\n- Dan Schneider is the co-president of the television production company Schneider's Bakery.\n- Dan Schneider created or co-created All That, The Amanda Show, What I Like About You, Drake & Josh, Zoey 101, iCarly, Victorious, Sam & Cat, Henry Danger, Game Shakers, and The Adventures of Kid Danger and Captain Man.\n- Helen Hunt has won four Emmy Awards, four Golden Globe Awards, and two Screen Actors Guild Awards.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
